Z||000000||87 Steve GT||02-13-2000||09:32 PM||||How hard is it to go from Auto to Standard??? Is there really too much involved???  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Standard||02-14-2000||01:23 AM||||You will need a new EMC, don't know about the wiring harness.  New console, I think.. shift cables, tranny mounts, other misc. things.  I don't think it would be worth it unless you're swapping the engine at the same time.||||reg||1
Z||000002||wkayl||02-14-2000||01:47 AM||||????Did manual tranny Fieros come with cruise control?  I was told they didn't.  But then I've ben told a lot of things that turned out to be bunk.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Patrick||02-14-2000||02:01 AM||||<BR>Yeah, and don't forget about the great hydraulic system. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> Master cylinder, slave cylinder, and all the lines that connect them.<P>You might want to simply find a Fiero that came from the factory as a standard. It would save you from a ton of work and expense... ||||reg||1
Z||000004||fiero56||02-14-2000||08:11 AM||||wkayl,<BR>cruise control was available on both automatics and standards.||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||02-14-2000||09:43 AM||||Standard, you don't need a new ECM, just the correct PROM. Warning Not all PROMS and ECM get along. You have to know what PROMS fit what year (part number) ECM.<P>Yes, the shift suround is deferant from auto to stick. The rest of the consol is the same.<P>If the auto tranny car has cruise you'll also need the wiring that goes to the clutch or cruise won't work right and could even wreck the car.<P>||||reg||1
